From: Graeme Winter <graeme.winter@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usbip: usbipd: enable TCP keepalive on exported connections

The client enables SO_KEEPALIVE in usbip_net_tcp_connect(), but usbipd
never does so on the accepted connection. If a client disappears without
closing its socket (power loss, cable pulled, network partition) the stub
driver keeps the device in the "used" state indefinitely, and it cannot
be imported again until it is unbound and rebound by hand.

Enable keepalive on the server side as well. Together with short
net.ipv4.tcp_keepalive_* settings the dead connection is detected, the
socket errors out in the stub driver, and the device becomes available
for import again.

Signed-off-by: Graeme Winter <graeme.winter@gmail.com>
---
 tools/usb/usbip/src/usbipd.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/tools/usb/usbip/src/usbipd.c b/tools/usb/usbip/src/usbipd.c
index 48398a7..d89633d 100644
--- a/tools/usb/usbip/src/usbipd.c
+++ b/tools/usb/usbip/src/usbipd.c
@@ -119,6 +119,7 @@ static int recv_request_import(int sockfd)
 	if (found) {
 		/* should set TCP_NODELAY for usbip */
 		usbip_net_set_nodelay(sockfd);
+		usbip_net_set_keepalive(sockfd);
 
 		/* export device needs a TCP/IP socket descriptor */
 		status = usbip_export_device(edev, sockfd);
